const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Chapter 7, we're finally done with the group of six and take a look at a trio now.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#The_Lion,_the_Mouse,_and_the_Monkey\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Lion, the Mouse, and the Monkey</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Friendship_or_Duty?\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Friendship or Duty?</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#The_Strength_of_Solitude\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Strength of Solitude</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#The_Witch&#39;s_Den\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Witch's Den</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"The_Lion.2C_the_Mouse.2C_and_the_Monkey\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Lion,_the_Mouse,_and_the_Monkey\">The Lion, the Mouse, and the Monkey</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Lion, the Mouse, and the Monkey\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_16?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Lion, the Mouse, and the Monkey\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Well, new character time as always!\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Squall_Leonhart_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Squall Leonhart (Dissidia PSP)\">Squall</a></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d9/Dissidia_Squall.png/revision/latest?cb=20101216073753\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Dissidia Squall\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d9/Dissidia_Squall.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/175?cb=20101216073753\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"175\" height=\"261\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Dissidia Squall.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissidia_Squall.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Squall is back from FF8, and as always is cold, quiet and professional. Unfortunately his story is one they didn't carry over well, Squall's character arc in FF8 was him being torn between his duties as a mercenary and what he knew was right which conflicted with his duties, and his coping mechanism for dealing with the world, that is complete emotional detachment, broke down as his personal universe tore at the seams, forcing him to re-evaluate his life. Here, he's cold and impersonal for no given reason, but he still has a good heart. He goes off alone and leaves his friends behind, but declares they still fight together. He abandons them and doesn't go back to save them when he knows they're in trouble, but says he still cares about them and considers them friends... Yeah. The morals of the next three chapters are all a bit confusing, I'll discuss this as we proceed.\n</p><p>Squall is another melee-focused fighter, but he has a lot of spell attacks, in fact he has five spells to four sword combos. Yup, Squall only has two melee attacks on ground or in the air. However, they're all he needs. Squall is an absolute <i>beast</i> in Bravery damage, Solid Barrel and Beat Fang do incredible damage, and Upper Blues and Heel Crush give him a bit of versatility to save him from being completely predictable. His spell attacks, contrary to the lines of Cloud and Tidus who have ranged moves solely so they have ranged moves, are as vital a part of his arsenal as his melee blows, setting opponents up for them and doing a fair bit of damage in their own right. However, Squall has a crushing weakness...his HP attacks are <i>slow</i> as can be, and very easy to avoid. You have to rely on Assists or his spells to set up for them, not a problem against the dumb AI in this chapter but later, it's a big hassle. Still, his potent Bravery attacks make him so powerful you won't need to land many HP hits to finish off the enemy. And in his EX Mode, oh god...but we'll get to that when I cover his EX Mode during the chapter.\n</p><p>Squall starts off with Upper Blues, an uppercut that has him dash forward a short distance, then he leaps up and performs a few more attacks to slam the opponent into the ground, and Blizzard Barret, a basic ice shot at the opponent. His aerial moves are Beat Fang, a fast-hitting combo attack that slams the opponent into the ground, and Heel Crush, a spinning attack forward to strike once and, you guessed it, make the opponent kiss the dirt. His HP attacks are Rough Divide, where he pauses then dashes at the opponent, rising or descending on an angle to strike, and Aerial Circle, where he swings to create explosive orbs in a vertical ring around him, then detonates them. He also moves towards the opponent during the swing and always creates the ring in a way to hit the opponent based on their current position. It also has Magic Block, preventing projectiles from stopping you during the execution.\n</p><p>Squall is overall a very powerful character with strengths far outweighing his flaws in my opinion, but he <i>is</i> flawed and you have to learn how to make up for them. Use him well.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>I gave Squall a Nodachi, Shell Shield, Green Beret and Silken Shirt. For accessories the customary Hyper Ring, Muscle Belt and Sunrise, but for boosters I opted for HP = 100%, Empty Assist Gauge and Level 1-9, as Squall never has an Assist in his tale. And now, we launch!\n</p><p>As we open, Squall has apparently saved Bartz and Zidane from some enemies up in the northern areas. However, he declines their offer to accompany them, and Bartz gives Squall his Chocobo Feather good luck charm to take with him for help on his journey.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Physical Critical Rate Up\"><img alt=\"Physical Critical Rate Up\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Thief\"><img alt=\"Capricious Thief\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Witch\"><img alt=\"Transient Witch\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Lion\"><img alt=\"Transient Lion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Valor Incense\"><img alt=\"Valor Incense\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Guess what Chain to use and where! Straight Chain at A3 where you begin you say? Good boy, have an e-cookie! The KP Chance is a 90 second win. The blue emblem is a Physical Critical Rate Up, if you lack a Straight Chain use a Jump Chain on it to get three enemies.\n</p><p>First is a Transient Lion with Upper Blues, Heel Crush, and Aerial Circle. Next comes a Transient Witch with Knight's Axe. Now comes the hard enemy, a Transient Gunner with Richochet Shot, Homing Bazooka and Satellite Laser, and the Typhon summon. It also has the accessory gimmick of the story, 8 BRV ≥ Base Value boosters with a White Cape or a Protect Stud, giving them a an 8x booster level for a total 24% boost to magic or physical defense when they have higher Bravery than their base. It sounds impressive, but the second you land a Bravery attack doing even 1 damage those boosters turn off, so it's pretty lame. It also doesn't make sense to give some enemies White Capes when the <i>really</i> powerful moves Squall uses are physical blows, and that build only uses 9 slots anyway so why not use the Cape and Stud together? The last foe is a Capricious Thief with Scoop Art, Solution 9, Shift Break, the Giant of Babil summon, and the White Cape and booster accessory build.\n</p><p>The chest has a useless Arcane Incense for us.\n</p><p>As we leave and appear on the world map, Zidane and Bartz are still running around. Turn around and approach the rock on the shoreline. An annoying little problem Squall has is that his world map attack, Solid Barrel, has him take a step back, and the rock doesn't shatter until he does the last part of the attack, so if you aren't right up next the rock, Squall will attack twice, then step back and the third strike will miss and the rock remains intact. Get closer and try again, ugh. The island the beam connects to has a chest with 1000 gil, and despite being large has nothing else on the two ends. Back on the mainland approach the sealed gateway in view for another 1000 gil. Go through the mountains to find Zidane near a rock, shatter it to create a long grindbar to an island with 2000 gil. Also Zidane has a funny line if you chat with him. Go back to where you appeared and head to the shoreline to find a Capricous Reaper to take out, it's level 17 but a first strike and its three Cursed Rings will sap its level advantage.\n</p><p>Squall hit Level 3 from this fight and learned Solid Barrel. It has much less range than Upper Blues but does more than twice as much damage, and begins a Chase, the only one of Squall's melee blows to do so, so when the time comes to charge up that EX Gauge later on, guess what move I hope you know how to use well. At the far end of the beach is a Maser Eye. Now just go to the next gateway, not hard to find, just watch for the dark smoke rising over the mountains. Near it is a chest with another Arcane Incense.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imitation Liegeman\"><img alt=\"Imitation Liegeman\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /