asy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fallacious Tree\"><img alt=\"Fallacious Tree\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest?cb=20100712153022\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Alexander (AUTO)\"><img alt=\"Alexander (AUTO)\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Summonstone.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Summonstone.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20100712153022\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Booster Accessory multiplier x5\"><img alt=\"Booster Accessory multiplier x5\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter we get a neat call to how Squall knew Laguna in FF8 and the state of Laguna now. Multichain at C6 to nail six enemies, activating the Booster x5 emblem. Sadly all I had were two Jump Chains so I used one at A3 to get two, yeah it technically loses KP given the cost of a Jump Chain, but meh, I have two so why not? The KP Chance is a 90 second win, and the bonus line is 4.\n</p><p>First, a Fallacious Tree, it uses Hurricane and Delta Attack, Rough Divide is a good counter for both since it will pierce the attack to hit while he can't move. The Strange enemy is an Imitation Liegeman, he comes into the fray with a lot of Bravery, calls Cactuar, then spams Straightarrow, once again his summon is kinda pointless since he doesn't use any attacks that can Break you. Sure it'll save him one time, but one time is it. The Hard enemy guarding the summonstone is a Transient Gunner with the White Cape set-up, Ricochet Shot, Homing Bazooka and Satellite Laser. The foe on F1 is an Ephemeral Summoner with Heavenly Strike and Thor's Hammer, and the inaccessible enemy on F3 is a Transient Lion fond of Aerial Circle and its ground variant, Fated Circle.\n</p><p>The summon is Alexander, when called he freezes your Bravery in place, preventing it from increasing or being damaged, and letting you spam HP attacks at full power. He's one of many ways to break the game's superboss, as anyone who has seen my YouTube account can attest, but on his own on normal enemies, not too awesome, he usually won't last long enough for you to get more than two uses out of him.\n</p><p>As we leave, Cosmos appears to Squall, who tells him his choice to go it alone without Zidane and Bartz was a wise decision, as he has to face Ultimecia alone. However, some rather unsubtle foreshadowing shows not all is as it seems.\n</p><p>Welcome to the desert, a big place. The ruined tower hides a chest with 1000 gil, and near the inactive gateway is a chest with Iifa Dew. There's also one of two Fallacious Trees here, an easy win. Far to the right of the inactivate gateway at the edge of the desert is a Rosetta Stone. Head to the next Tree, hard to miss given it's bright blue, and in an alcove nearby is a chest with 1999 gil. You can also head to an outcropping over to the sea to snag a KP Gambler, can never have too many of those...well you can, but it's still good to have more than one. Head back into the desert and go to the gateway, there's a chest on your right on the path with a Valor Resin. Buy a Multichain from the moogle if you lack one. He also has some new boosters and summons for sale, the boosters aren't much use, but the summons, Bahamut and Leviathan should be your main purchases if you're looking to spend.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Friendship_or_Duty.3F\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Friendship_or_Duty?\">Friendship or Duty?</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Friendship or Duty?\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_16?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Friendship or Duty?\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\