alfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Lion\"><img alt=\"Transient Lion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/D012_Cosmos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110325134317\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Warrior of Light\"><img alt=\"Warrior of Light\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"24\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Cosmos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Cosmos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/D012_Cosmos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/24?cb=20110325134317\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fleeting Flash\"><img alt=\"Fleeting Flash\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"><img alt=\"Initial Stage BRV Boost\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Witch\"><img alt=\"Transient Witch\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imitation Despot\"><img alt=\"Imitation Despot\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Revolver\"><img alt=\"Revolver\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Drakey hates blank spaces between templates, kiddies, reminds him he can't be as specific in regards to strategy in this game as he's used to. Anyway, Straight Chain at A2 to get four of them, I didn't have one so I used a Jump Chain at C4 to get three of them. The purple emblem there is a Initial Stage BRV Boost emblem, helping against the Expert a lot. The bonus line is 13 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win. Note the Hard enemies here are actually quite a step up from previous ones, they're Level 19 each instead of Level 12, and have Level 30 weapons for a higher offensive boost than previous ones.\n</p><p>First, a Fleeting Flash with Launch and Ruin. I spammed Solid Barrel and chase attacks to fill up my EX Gauge in preparation for the Expert enemy. The second enemy is a Transient Witch with Knight's Axe, Typhon, and the White Cape set-up. Now comes the Expert, an Imitation Despot with Light Crest, Thunder Crest, Flare, a Hyper Ring and Guardian Bangle boosted by 8 HP = 100% boosters, and the Tonberry summon. After a set of time when he's called, Tonberry does Bravery damage to you equal to however much HP the summoner has lost, and it will Break you if the HP loss is high enough. This Expert piece is pretty easy to kill though, Aerial Circle will block his Light Crest projectiles, and with EX Mode Squall can quickly Break him, getting the stage Bravery which will surely be high enough to deal a one-hit KO. Don't use an EX Burst, save the bit of gauge you have left at the end to refill for the boss. With him gone the foes left are a False Hero with Dayflash, Blue Fang, and Crossover, and a Transient Lion with Blizzard Barret, Fusillade, Mystic Flurry, a White Cape set-up, and Typhon.\n</p><p>The chest has Squall's trademark Revolver in it, but it has no special abilities and by this point you have plenty of high-end gear that do to choose from instead.\n</p><p>Squall learned Thunder Barret from these fights. It's his key spell, Squall creates a line of lightning in front of him, dragging opponents in front of him and out of the air. If it hits though the end lag is cancelled out, letting Squall quickly combo into another move while the opponent is helpless before him. Thunder Barret to Solid Barrel is a brutal combo that helps compensate for the latter's crap range, and while the longer start-up makes the timing tighter, you can also combo Thunder Barret into the HP attacks Fated Circle (which you'll learn soon) or Blasting Zone (ditto). \n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Warrior_of_Light_(Dissidia)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Warrior of Light (Dissidia)\">Warrior of Light</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d3/WoLDissidiaModel.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110706100935\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"WoLDissidiaModel\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"195\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"WoLDissidiaModel.PNG\" data-image-key=\"WoLDissidiaModel.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d3/WoLDissidiaModel.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110706100935\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,101\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">20\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">324\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Dayflash, Blue Fang, Ascension, Crossover, Shield Strike, Rising Buckler\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Ultimate Shield, Shining Wave, Shield of Light, Radiant Sword, Bitter End, Rune Saber\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we reach the end, Squall runs across the Warrior of Light. The Warrior questions his choice to travel alone, and Squall aptly points out the Warrior himself is alone, declaring he won't be dissuaded. So, now they have to fight. Why? I don't know.\n</p><p>The Warrior comes into battle with a Flametongue, giving him an initial Bravery boost on top of his level advantage. He's got a pretty nice accessory build, 3 Attacking Bravery and 4 Near Opponent pumping up a Power Ring. I'd have opted for a Hyper Ring or a Muscle Belt, but hey, it's decent. He's got HP links for all his aerial attacks and his ground attack Ascension, Radiant Sword to send six swords of light homing in on you, Shield of Light to block and punish your Bravery attacks, and Dayflash as a quick ground attack to get you out of his face. His summon is...I'm not really sure, he never used it.\n</p><p>The problem is, as always...yup, EX Mode. Use that new Thunder Barret to drag him in and slam him with an EX Mode Solid Barrel to Break him, then enter chase and wall rush him to knock off 2000 HP within the first ten seconds. Now just land another Solid Barrel, HP attack and EX Burst to end it. The Warrior is decently aggressive and has a good set-up for moves and equipment, he just can't stand up to the brute power of Squall's EX Mode bonus.\n</p><p>Squall got to Level 12 from this fight and learned Fated Circle, a ground version of Aerial Circle that creates orbs horizontally. It combos well with Thunder Barret as I said.\n</p><p>The Warrior is impressed with Squall's power, and wonders why he doesn't use that power to help protect his friends. Good question, since Squall knows other villains are actively pursuing them. Squall responds by saying that even if they're apart, they can support each other, and shows him Bartz's chocobo feather, claiming that they support him in their own way and he's returning the favor. That...really doesn't answer the question, and is a weak argument in itself. The Warrior sees he has misjudged Squall, thinking he preferred to be alone because he didn't trust his allies...which was never the case, and Squall never said so. The Warrior departs, reminding Squall he isn't alone, something Squall clearly already believes, no matter how bullshit an argument he formulated to express this. Why didn't they just have this chat before the fight? I dunno, like I said kiddies, this chapter's morals are all screwed up. \n</p><p>Remember kiddies, if your friends are being pursued by an androgynous mage intent on trapping them, it's best to ignore the danger to them and just have faith that they'll be okay, because they have faith in you. That's the <i>true</i> meaning of friendship. And now because I know you were all thinking it - \"Squall, don't believe in yourself, believe in them! Believe in the friends that believe in you!\"...ya know it makes a lot more sense phrased as Kamina said it. I guess the shades just have that effect.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"The_Witch.27s_Den\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Witch's_Den\">The Witch's Den</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Witch&#39;s Den\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_16?action=edit&amp;section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Witch&#39;s Den\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span cla