\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Witch\"><img alt=\"Transient Witch\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ultimecia\"><img alt=\"Ultimecia\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter, Cosmos appears and reveals herself as Ultimecia, who accuses Squall of being an untrusting jerk who abandoned Zidane and Bartz to Kuja's traps, which he did. Now that he's come so far it's time to take her down, but for some reason, Squall lowers his sword. Ultimecia then randomly decides that putting it off is cool with her, so she vanishes. We then get a scene of her speaking to Garland.\n</p><p>Multichain at B2 to get four enemies, the purple emblem granting an extra KP per fight. The enemy on the far right can be skipped. The bonus line is 16 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win. Remember to fill up that EX Gauge for the final battle!\n</p><p>First up, a Fallacious Wanderer with Solid Ascension, Rush Impact and Hellfire. Next a Transient Witch with Knight's Axe and Great Attractor. Now it's a Transient Gunner with Shotgun, Ragnarok Blade, a False Hero Assist, a Protect Stud set-up, and an unknown summon. Finally, an Imitation Liegeman as the Strange foe. It comes into the fight with a Bravery boost, has Rope Knife and Straightarrow, and uses the Cactuar summon. The enemy on the far right, if you really want to kill everything in sight, is a Phantasmal Harlequin with Meteor and Hyperdrive.\n</p><p>At the end of the stage, Squall confronts Ultimecia, who rolls out Garland to tag team Squall. Squall spews some more confusing double talk about how he can fight alone because he's not alone, he has friends who support him by not being here! Squall postures that he'll just beat both of them, then Zidane shows up to steal his thunder, tackling Garland to the side. Well, that leaves a bit of one-on-one for Squall then. A pity for Ultimecia her power over time only works in cutscenes or else this fight would be over literally before it started.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Ultimecia_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Ultimecia (Dissidia PSP)\">Ultimecia</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/9/9b/UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110822193930\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"151\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/9/9b/UltimeciaDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/120?cb=20110822193930\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,475\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">22\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">325\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Knight's Blade, Knight's Axe, Knight's Spear, Knight's Arrow\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Shockwave Pulsar, Great Attractor, Apocalypse\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Brynhildr\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Ultimecia came well equipped with a full moveset, and a False Stalwart for an Assist. She's back Brynhildr, though it'll probably help you more than her, and has a good accessory set. She's got on a Hyper Ring with four Far from Opponent, two Aerial, a Near Loss, and an Iifa Leaf. The Leaf, if you never used one yourself, gives her the Last Chance ability - the attack that will normally kill her, one time will just sap her to 1 HP, even an EX Burst. It also doesn't matter how much HP she has before hand, as long as she has more than 1 HP without using Last Chance already, it'll save her.\n</p><p>Even without EX Mode, Ultimecia is, once again, an anti-climax boss. She's pretty stupid and just flat weak. She tends to spam Knight's Axe the entire fight, which is very easy to block uncharged and easy to dodge when charged. Aside from a Knight's Spear counter when you wall rush her, she has no real signs of intelligence. If she used Knight's Blade or Knight's Arrow more maybe, but as is she's pathetic. Her HP attacks are perfect chances to smash into her with a Rouge Divide - she has the ability to move during Apocalypse but the AI has her hold in place, a fatal mistake. And for her normal blows, remember Aerial Circle and Fated Circle block magic attacks, and the only attacks of Ultimecia's that can pierce that are a charged Axe or Spear, and the Circle will detonate before she can get them off. The only complication is one of nuisance, Last Chance, all it means is that you have to sap her to 1 HP first if you plan to do the typical EX Burst finishing blow.\n</p><p>With the time witch faded away, Squall receives his Crystal and joins up with Zidane to go look for Bartz, who has apparently been captured.\n</p><p>As a final footnote, Squall hit Level 16 from the fight and got Blasting Zone. He extends a column of energy up into the air and then slams it down, dragging aerial opponents down and doing a bit of Bravery damage. He also turns on start-up to track the opponent, and its good reach and fast chop make it pretty effective as an anti-air attack.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 15\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthro